cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use benchprobe, cite the study it ships with and this repository by version."
title: "benchprobe: the analysis code behind One Capability or Many? and Three Ways Classical Test Theory Misleads for LLM Judges"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhu
    given-names: Louis Yiven
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-5579-0340"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/louisyzhu/benchprobe"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code extracted from the archives of two evaluation studies and packaged so the same
  computation runs by one command: reliability and grader-agreement estimators (trust), factor
  structure and incremental validity (measure), leave-one-benchmark-out prediction with bootstrap
  uncertainty (predict), and the one-command reproduction of the twelve archived One Capability
  result tables with per-table reproducibility tiers (report).
references:
  - type: article
    title: "One Capability or Many? Testing the Economic Validity of Frontier AI Evaluation"
    authors:
